ion":"","verse_key":"6:92"}]},{"verse_key":"6:93","surah":6,"ayah":93,"ar_uthmani":"وَمَنْ أَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ ٱفْتَرَىٰ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ كَذِبًا أَوْ قَالَ أُوحِىَ إِلَىَّ وَلَمْ يُوحَ إِلَيْهِ شَىْءٌ وَمَن قَالَ سَأُنزِلُ مِثْلَ مَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ ۗ وَلَوْ تَرَىٰٓ إِذِ ٱلظَّـٰلِمُونَ فِى غَمَرَٰتِ ٱلْمَوْتِ وَٱلْمَلَـٰٓئِكَةُ بَاسِطُوٓا۟ أَيْدِيهِمْ أَخْرِجُوٓا۟ أَنفُسَكُمُ ۖ ٱلْيَوْمَ تُجْزَوْنَ عَذَابَ ٱلْهُونِ بِمَا كُنتُمْ تَقُولُونَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ غَيْرَ ٱلْحَقِّ وَكُنتُمْ عَنْ ءَايَـٰتِهِۦ تَسْتَكْبِرُونَ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Who could be more wicked than someone who invents a lie against God, or claims, ‘A revelation has come to me,’ when no revelation has been sent to him, or says, ‘I too can reveal something equal to God’s revelation’? If you could only see the wicked in their death agonies, as the angels stretch out their hands [to them], saying, ‘Give up your souls. Today you will be repaid with a humiliating punishment for saying false things about God and for arrogantly rejecting His revelations.’","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَمَنْ","en_gloss":"And who","transliteration":"waman","verse_key":"6:93"},{"pos":2,"ar":"أَظْلَمُ","en_gloss":"(is) more unjust","transliteration":"aẓlamu","verse_key":"6:93"},{"pos":3,"ar":"مِمَّنِ","en_gloss":"than (one) who","transliteration":"mimmani","verse_key":"6:93"},{"pos":4,"ar":"ٱفْتَرَىٰ","en_gloss":"invents","transliteration":"if'tarā","verse_key":"6:93"},{"pos":5,"ar":"عَلَى","en_gloss":"about","transliteration":"ʿalā","verse_key":"6:93"},{"pos":6,"ar":"ٱللَّهِ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-lahi","verse_key":"6:93"},{"pos":7,"ar":"كَذِبًا","en_gloss":"a lie","transliteration":"kadhiban","verse_key":"6:93"},{"pos":8,"ar":"أَوْ","en_gloss":"or","transliteration":"aw","verse_key":"6:93"},{"pos":9,"ar":"قَالَ","en_gloss":"said","transliteration":"qāla","verse_key":"6:93"},{"pos":10,"ar":"أُوحِىَ","en_gloss":"It has been inspired","transliteration":"ūḥiya","verse_key":"6:93"},{"pos":11,"ar":"إِلَىَّ","en_glos